    "created_at": "2018-08-20T14:15:04Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-08-20T14:15:04Z",
    "body": "@reillyeon @krockot @odejesush Is this still preferred way how to comment the WebUSB standard?\r\n\r\nWe are producing a hardware that is used by several hundred thousand people all around the world and we are considering switching to WebUSB exclusively. Actually, everything is done on our side of things, we are just re-evaluating our decision, because of the removed whitelist interface. (It was part of the spec when we started to implement WebUSB).\r\n\r\nBecause our device is security oriented, we don't want any website to be able to communicate with it and we don't want to leave the competence of choosing the correct origin solely to the user. Having a whitelist would be certainly great! Please reconsider adding it back. Having it optional is perfectly fine.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
