    "created_at": "2018-08-20T15:21:15Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-08-20T16:18:25Z",
    "body": "I think that authentication pairing is orthogonal to origin whitelist. Pairing again puts an extra burden on user, becase they need to know against which app the pairing is happening. From user's perspective it's almost the same as current state. From phishing we know, users are not very good at telling the difference between legit and malicious origins.\r\n\r\nIf vendor going out of business is an issue (I understood that's one of the main concern in #49), it might be worth to introduce an advanced-setting flag in browser, which can turn off this origin check for particular device. Sacrificing this security feature completely just for the hypothetical case of vendor going out of business behind is bad IMHO.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
