    "created_at": "2018-09-13T22:23:53Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-09-13T22:23:53Z",
    "body": "This implies non-trivial requirements on the device - it needs to support asymmetric cryptography. It's not a problem for our token, but for others, it might be a problem.\r\n\r\nAnother issue is that the server needs to keep some kind of a secret and have an active signer component, which makes it much harder to deploy such service (e.g. you can't host your website from static hosting such as Github pages). Or one could solve that via SSL certs and PKI, but having complete PKI implemented in the device is almost impossible.\r\n\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
